### API

```tsx
// Basic usage
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom error handler (e.g. Sentry)
<ErrorBoundary onError={(error, info) => Sentry.captureException(error)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback UI
<ErrorBoundary fallback={({ error, retry }) => (
  <div>
    <p>{error.message}</p>
    <button onClick={retry}>Retry</button>
  </div>
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

### Key design decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| Class component | React only supports `componentDidCatch` / `getDerivedStateFromError` in class components |
| Render-prop `fallback` | More flexible than a static element — gives consumers access to `error`, `errorInfo`, and `retry` |
| `onError` prop | Lets callers plug in any logger (Sentry, Datadog, etc.) without coupling the component to one |
| `retry` resets state to `null` | Clears the error so children re-render on the next render cycle |
